§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses”„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ©Wherefore Nathan spake unto Bath-sheba the mother of Solomon, saying, Hast thou not heard that Adonijah the son of Haggith doth reign, and David our lord knoweth it not?¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ‚Now therefore come, let me, I pray thee, give thee counsel, that thou mayest save thine own life, and the life of thy son Solomon.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙèGo and get thee in unto king David, and say unto him, Didst not thou, my lord, O king, swear unto thine handmaid, saying, Assuredly Solomon thy son shall reign after me, and he shall sit upon my throne? why then doth Adonijah reign?¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙjBehold, while thou yet talkest there with the king, I also will come in after thee, and confirm thy words.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book
§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses—„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ†And Bath-sheba went in unto the king into the chamber: and the king was very old; and Abishag the Shunammite ministered unto the king.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ]And Bath-sheba bowed, and did obeisance unto the king. And the king said, What wouldest thou?¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ®And she said unto him, My lord, thou swarest by the LORD thy God unto thine handmaid, saying, Assuredly Solomon thy son shall reign after me, and he shall sit upon my throne.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙSAnd now, behold, Adonijah reigneth; and now, my lord the king, thou knowest it not:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÎand he hath slain oxen and fat cattle and sheep in abundance, and hath called all the sons of the king, and Abiathar the priest, and Joab the captain of the host: but Solomon thy servant hath he not called.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ™And thou, my lord, O king, the eyes of all Israel are upon thee, that thou shouldest tell them who shall sit on the throne of my lord the king after him.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙŠOtherwise it shall come to pass, when my lord the king shall sleep with his fathers, that I and my son Solomon shall be counted offenders.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book
§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses–„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙMAnd, lo, while she yet talked with the king, Nathan the prophet also came in.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¡And they told the king, saying, Behold Nathan the prophet. And when he was come in before the king, he bowed himself before the king with his face to the ground.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙqAnd Nathan said, My lord, O king, hast thou said, Adonijah shall reign after me, and he shall sit upon my throne?¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÚFor he is gone down this day, and hath slain oxen and fat cattle and sheep in abundance, and hath called all the king's sons, and the captains of the host, and Abiathar the priest; and, behold, they eat and drink before him, and say, God save king Adonijah.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ€But me, even me thy servant, and Zadok the priest, and Benaiah the son of Jehoiada, and thy servant Solomon, hath he not called.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ‘Is this thing done by my lord the king, and thou hast not shewed it unto thy servant, who should sit on the throne of my lord the king after him?¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book
§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses”„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙxThen king David answered and said, Call me Bath-sheba. And she came into the king's presence, and stood before the king.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙaAnd the king sware, and said, As the LORD liveth, that hath redeemed my soul out of all distress,¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¿even as I sware unto thee by the LORD God of Israel, saying, Assuredly Solomon thy son shall reign after me, and he shall sit upon my throne in my stead; even so will I certainly do this day.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ€Then Bath-sheba bowed with her face to the earth, and did reverence to the king, and said, Let my lord king David live for ever.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book
§chapter«first_verse ªlast_verse%¦verses–„¥verse ¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ†And king David said, Call me Zadok the priest, and Nathan the prophet, and Benaiah the son of Jehoiada. And they came before the king.¦layout ªlast_verse „¥verse!¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ˜The king also said unto them, Take with you the servants of your lord, and cause Solomon my son to ride upon mine own mule, and bring him down to Gihon:¦layout ªlast_verse!„¥verse"¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙand let Zadok the priest and Nathan the prophet anoint him there king over Israel: and blow ye with the trumpet, and say, God save king Solomon.¦layout ªlast_verse"„¥verse#¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¬Then ye shall come up after him, that he may come and sit upon my throne; for he shall be king in my stead: and I have appointed him to be ruler over Israel and over Judah.¦layout ªlast_verse#„¥verse$¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙoAnd Benaiah the son of Jehoiada answered the king, and said, Amen: the LORD God of my lord the king say so too.¦layout ªlast_verse$„¥verse%¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ‹As the LORD hath been with my lord the king, even so be he with Solomon, and make his throne greater than the throne of my lord king David.¦layout ªlast_verse%…¤book
§chapter«first_verse&ªlast_verse(¦verses“„¥verse&¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÎSo Zadok the priest, and Nathan the prophet, and Benaiah the son of Jehoiada, and the Cherethites, and the Pelethites, went down, and caused Solomon to ride upon king David's mule, and brought him to Gihon.¦layout ªlast_verse&„¥verse'¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ And Zadok the priest took an horn of oil out of the tabernacle, and anointed Solomon. And they blew the trumpet; and all the people said, God save king Solomon.¦layout ªlast_verse'„¥verse(¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ’And all the people came up after him, and the people piped with pipes, and rejoiced with great joy, so that the earth rent with the sound of them.¦layout ªlast_verse(…¤book
§chapter«first_verse)ªlast_verse0¦verses˜„¥verse)¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÍAnd Adonijah and all the guests that were with him heard it as they had made an end of eating. And when Joab heard the sound of the trumpet, he said, Wherefore is this noise of the city being in an uproar?¦layout ªlast_verse)„¥verse*¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ©And while he yet spake, behold, Jonathan the son of Abiathar the priest came: and Adonijah said unto him, Come in; for thou art a valiant man, and bringest good tidings.¦layout ªlast_verse*„¥verse+¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ^And Jonathan answered and said to Adonijah, Verily our lord king David hath made Solomon king.¦layout ªlast_verse+„¥verse,¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÊAnd the king hath sent with him Zadok the priest, and Nathan the prophet, and Benaiah the son of Jehoiada, and the Cherethites, and the Pelethites, and they have caused him to ride upon the king's mule:¦layout ªlast_verse,„¥verse-¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ»and Zadok the priest and Nathan the prophet have anointed him king in Gihon: and they are come up from thence rejoicing, so that the city rang again. This is the noise that ye have heard.¦layout ªlast_verse-„¥verse.¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ6And also Solomon sitteth on the throne of the kingdom.¦layout ªlast_verse.„¥verse/¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÔAnd moreover the king's servants came to bless our lord king David, saying, God make the name of Solomon better than thy name, and make his throne greater than thy throne. And the king bowed himself upon the bed.¦layout ªlast_verse/„¥verse0¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙŒAnd also thus said the king, Blessed be the LORD God of Israel, which hath given one to sit on my throne this day, mine eyes even seeing it.¦layout ªlast_verse0…¤book
§chapter«first_verse1ªlast_verse1¦verses‘„¥verse1¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ`And all the guests that were with Adonijah were afraid, and rose up, and went every man his way.¦layout ªlast_verse1…¤book
§chapter«first_verse2ªlast_verse5¦verses”„¥verse2¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙgAnd Adonijah feared because of Solomon, and arose, and went, and caught hold on the horns of the altar.¦layout ªlast_verse2„¥verse3¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙßAnd it was told Solomon, saying, Behold, Adonijah feareth king Solomon: for, lo, he hath caught hold on the horns of the altar, saying, Let king Solomon swear unto me to day that he will not slay his servant with the sword.¦layout ªlast_verse3„¥verse4¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ And Solomon said, If he will shew himself a worthy man, there shall not an hair of him fall to the earth: but if wickedness shall be found in him, he shall die.¦layout ªlast_verse4„¥verse5¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙœSo king Solomon sent, and they brought him down from the altar. And he came and bowed himself to king Solomon: and Solomon said unto him, Go to thine house.¦layout ªlast_verse5